# Freally MIDI Master — the novelty guard's reference table (FR-011, TASK-039)
#
# ⛔ HASHES ONLY. Each line is a 64-bit fingerprint of a *contour* — a run of
# (interval, onset-gap) steps — and there is no way back from one to a note.
# Nothing here names a pitch, a key, a tempo or a title. That is the point:
# this table ships inside a product that must never carry somebody else's
# notes.
#
# ⛔ DO NOT HAND-EDIT. Rebuild it:
#
#     cargo run -p datasetc -- novelty <contours>/ > data/novelty/hooks.hash
#
# where <contours>/ holds one `*.contour` listing per melody. Those listings
# are an input and are deliberately NOT in this repo — see
# docs/dataset-protocol.md § The novelty table, which records the format, the
# melody list this file was built from, and why the inputs stay out.
#
# Built at fingerprint scheme 1, at both widths the guard looks up: n = 8
# (the screen every take must pass) and n = 12 (the loosened screen).
#
# The set below is a public-domain starter set — seven traditional and
# classical melodies — and it is expected to grow. It is what makes the guard
# a working mechanism today rather than a switch waiting to be wired.

